# Template for --data-roots-file (loader.apply_data_roots) -- a flat YAML
# mapping of NAME: value, no hostname-keying (deliberately, see that
# function's own docstring: "each machine only ever reads its OWN file",
# avoiding machines.yaml's confirmed-stale-entry bug class). Copy this file
# to the TARGET machine, rename it (data_roots.yaml, or anything you like),
# edit the values for THAT machine's real data layout, then pass it to the
# generated script:
#
#   python generated_nse.py --data-roots-file data_roots.yaml --start ... --stop ...
#
# (or to oceanicu_driver.py itself, same flag, if running from source instead
# of a --dump-python'd script). --data-root NAME=VALUE on the command line
# always wins over this file if you need a one-off override without editing
# it; an already-exported real env var always wins over this file too (only
# fills gaps, never clobbers a deliberate export).
#
# Values below are THIS machine's (the one this file was generated on) --
# a starting point, not necessarily correct for the target machine. Sorted
# into two groups:

# --- Likely personal/this-machine-only paths -- almost certainly need
# --- editing on the target machine unless it shares this exact home dir.
# The FULL, real path to wherever the domain's own bathymetry file actually
# lives -- since Bathymetry/ split per-domain (NSe/Bathymetry/, AMM7/
# Bathymetry/, ...), this needs updating per domain being run; one shared
# var name, not a per-domain-suffixed one, since only one real value is ever
# needed per run.
BATHYMETRY_FOLDER: /home/kb/source/repos/OceanICU/oceanicu_3d/NSe/Bathymetry
HYDROGRAPHY_FOLDER_CMEMS: /home/kb/source/repos/boundaries
BOUNDARY_FOLDER_BAROTROPIC_CMEMS: /home/kb/source/repos/boundaries/boundary_data
BOUNDARY_FOLDER_BAROCLINIC_CMEMS: /home/kb/source/repos/boundaries/boundary_data

# --- Possibly shared storage (/data, /server/data) -- check whether the
# --- target machine has these mounted/reachable at the same paths before
# --- assuming they're correct unedited.
TPXO_FOLDER: /server/data/TPXO9
# /data/WOA doesn't exist on orca -- confirmed directly, real path is
# /server/data/WOA (same /server/data share as TPXO_FOLDER above).
HYDROGRAPHY_FOLDER_WOA: /server/data/WOA
# boundaries.baroclinic.WOA's own folder -- the SAME real woa_t.nc/woa_s.nc
# climatology as HYDROGRAPHY_FOLDER_WOA above (independently settable, not
# reused automatically -- see oceanicu_providers.py's own WOA choice
# comment), so this needs the same real value.
BOUNDARY_FOLDER_BAROCLINIC_WOA: /server/data/WOA
BOUNDARY_FOLDER_BAROTROPIC_CMIP6: /data/CMIP6
BOUNDARY_FOLDER_BAROCLINIC_CMIP6: /data/CMIP6
# Parent of the real per-extraction subfolder ("kaj" -- meteo.ERA5.model,
# substituted via meteo.ERA5.folder_template) -- real files live at
# ERA5_FOLDER/kaj/era5_t2m_????.nc etc, not directly in ERA5_FOLDER itself.
ERA5_FOLDER: /data/ERA5
CMIP6_FOLDER: /data/BiasCorrected
RIVER_FOLDER: /data/EMORID
KD490_FOLDER: /data/Kd490
OUTPUT_FOLDER: .
